      "message": "That\u0027s not what this is checking - the check is for the IME **layering target**, i.e. the window that\u0027s using the IME.\n\nThe purpose of the existing check is to prevent lifting a dialog that is below the IME layering target onto the IME. \n\nExample: Let\u0027s consider the following windows (bottom to top):\n\n`NotificationShade` (FLAG_ALT_FOCUSABLE_IM) -\u003e `Wifi Password Dialog` (layering target) -\u003e `IME`\n\nWith your change, we would raise the NotificationShade onto the IME, making it unusable.",
